# drvlist

A FreeBSD tool to enumerate installed drives in a system
and display the most useful information in one go.

Author: Peter Eriksson <pen@lysator.liu.se>


Usage:
    ./drvlist [<options>] [<dev-1> [.. <dev-N>]

Options:
    -h              Display usage information
    -S <column>     Sort using column
    -C <columns>    Columns to display
    -W <width>      Force terminal width
    -D <level>      Enable internal debugging
    -F <separator>  Columns separator [ : ]
    -r              Reverse sort order
    -v              Enable (increase) verbose output
    -m              Enable multipath support

Notes:
   Columns for '-C' is a comma separated list optionally
   prefixed with '+' or '-' in order to add or remove columns

Columns:
    NAME VENDOR PRODUCT VERSION IDENT SIZE TEMP SMART
    TESTS HOURS WEAR MADE PROTO XPORT CTRL PATH
    PHYS

Version:
    2.0 (Built: Nov 25 2026 12:47:52)

